course: dictionary
lesson: 172
title: Looking back with ago
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ago means before now, back in the past. You put it after a time, as in «two years ago», to show how far back something happened.
explain: Count back from today to find the time. If something happened «two days ago», it happened two days before today. The number tells you how far back to look.
explain: Some phrases do not give a number but still point back: «long ago», «a while ago» and «not long ago». Ago always looks backwards, never forwards.
fact: Ago means before now, back in the past.
fact: «Thousands of years ago» means a very long time before today.
fact: «Long ago» is a phrase that points back to the past without giving an exact number.
fact: «Not long ago» means recently, a short time back from now.
fact: Ago looks back. To look forward, English uses words such as «in» or «later», as in «in two days».
exercise: «People in the Andes tamed guinea pigs thousands of years ago.» What does ago tell you? | Right now, this minute | *Before now, back in the past | Somewhere far away | After now, in the future
exercise: «Long ago tunnels were dug by hand with picks and shovels.» Where does long ago point? | Right now | To the next town | *Back in the past | Forward into the future
exercise: Sam says, «I finished my homework two days ago.» When did Sam finish? | Two days from today | Next week | Today | *Two days before today
test: «That was Paraceratherium, which lived about 30 million years ago.» Is this in the past, now, or the future? | *In the past | Tomorrow | In the future | Now
test: Ella says, «The guinea pigs reached Europe on ships about five hundred years ago.» Does Ella mean before now or after now? | *Before now | At this moment | Later today | After now
exam: Which phrase means a short time back from now? | in two days | next year | *not long ago | later on
